;__groto__ (Was Footnote:  ) El Grotto: x1 reflects El Grotto culture/nationality/language/geography in aspect x2: (Was Footnote: ((And)))
;__jamro__ (Was Footnote:  ) Aymara: x1 reflects Aymara culture in aspect x2 (Was Footnote: ((Adam)))
;__kadro__ (Was Footnote:  ) Ecuadorian: x1 reflects Ecuadorian culture/nationality/language/geography in aspect x2
;__kamro__ (Was Footnote:  ) Welsh: x1 reflects Welsh culture/nationality/language/geography in aspect x2 (Was Footnote: or ''kimro''): (Was Footnote: ((And)))
;__kasto__ (Was Footnote:  ) Spanish: x1 reflects culture/nationality/language/geography of Spain in aspect x2: (Was Footnote: ((And)))  ''Why not use spano?''  For same reason as reason for using ''glano'' alongside ''glico''. ((And))  ''It should probably be the other way around: ''kasto'' for the language and ''spano'' for the country. I suspect that using ''kasto'' for the whole of Spain would be too politically incorrect. It would be like using ''glico'' for the whole UK.'' ((xorxes))
;__kepko__ (Was Footnote:  kek ) Québécois: x1 reflects Québécois culture/nationality/language/geography in aspect x2 (Was Footnote: ((pne)))Suggestions for better gismu? I'd like to use ''kebko'' but that has a problem with voiced/unvoiced in the middle.
;__kimro__ (Was Footnote:  ) Welsh: x1 reflects Welsh culture/nationality/language/geography in aspect x2 (Was Footnote: or ''kamro'')
